97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (office towers. Lodging increased 13 basis points to 5.35%, reversing last month's improvement, as new hotel delinquencies outpaced a short list of cures. Retail increased just five basis points to 6.96%. $1.0 billion in newly delinquent retail balances were offset by four large regional malls that shifted from non-performing to performing matured balloon status during the month. Industrial posted the only decrease, declining seven basis points to 1.13%, as cures modestly outpaced limited new inflows.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (If loans past their maturity date but current on interest \(classified as performing matured balloon\) were included, the delinquency rate would register 9.62%, up nine basis points from June. This figure sits 176 basis points above the headline rate of 7.86%. The narrower gap versus prior months reflects maturity-related distress shifting out of performing matured balloon status and into non-performing matured balloon status, which is captured in the headline rate. The seriously delinquent rate \(60+ days delinquent, in foreclosure, real estate owned \(REO\), or non-performing matured balloon\) increased, rising to 7.57% from 7.16%.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The percentage of loan balance in the 30-day delinquent bucket is 0.29%, an increase of 10 basis points versus June \(0.19%\). )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
